{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7865591","formula":"C₂₀H₂₂N₂O₃","hill":"C20H22N2O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":22.0,"N":2.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"URB597"},"descriptions":{"en":"EX-597 (former developmental code names URB-597, KDS-4103, and ORG-231295) is a fatty acid amide hydrolase inhibitor (FAAH inhibitor) which is under development for the treatment of social anxiety disorder (or social phobia) and post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD). It is a relatively selective and irreversible inhibitor of the enzyme fatty acid amide hydrolase (FAAH). FAAH is the primary degradatory enzyme for the endocannabinoid anandamide and, as such, inhibition of FAAH leads to an accumulation of anandamide in the CNS and periphery where it activates cannabinoid receptors."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":1383884,"mass":338.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCC(CC1)NC(=O)OC2=CC=CC(=C2)C3=CC(=CC=C3)C(=O)N","inchikey":"ROFVXGGUISEHAM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"[3-(3-carbamoylphenyl)phenyl] N-cyclohexylcarbamate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1383884","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.704,"y":1.401,"z":-0.722,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.978,"y":0.789,"z":1.506,"el":"O"},{"x":2.84,"y":-3.409,"z":0.464,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.615,"y":0.372,"z":-0.085,"el":"N"},{"x":5.099,"y":-3.657,"z":0.158,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.584,"y":-0.268,"z":0.784,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.005,"y":0.025,"z":0.292,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.314,"y":-1.774,"z":0.855,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.345,"y":-0.707,"z":-1.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.659,"y":-2.499,"z":-0.445,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.087,"y":-2.206,"z":-0.892,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.396,"y":0.847,"z":0.353,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.449,"y":1.912,"z":-0.375,"el":"C"},{"x":1.896,"y":1.587,"z":-0.094,"el":"C"},{"x":0.645,"y":1.078,"z":-0.441,"el":"C"},{"x":3.065,"y":0.738,"z":-0.155,"el":"C"},{"x":